{"tool_name":"profia","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"profia","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/proFIA.html","license":"CECILL-2.1","summary":"Flow Injection Analysis coupled to High-Resolution Mass Spectrometry is a promising approach for high-throughput metabolomics. FIA-HRMS data, however, cannot be pre-processed with current software tools which rely on liquid chromatography separation, or handle low resolution data only. Here we present the package that implements a new methodology to pre-process FIA-HRMS raw data (netCDF, mzData, mzXML, and mzML) and generates the peak table.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:04:43Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:09:33.383343Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.0.10"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:profia","credit":[{"email":"alexis.delabriere@cea.fr","name":"Alexis Delabriere","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/proFIA.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Peak calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3222"}]}],"name":"proFIA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nmeth.3252","metadata":{"abstract":"Bioconductor is an open-source, open-development software project for the analysis and comprehension of high-throughput data in genomics and molecular biology. The project aims to enable interdisciplinary research, collaboration and rapid development of scientific software. Based on the statistical programming language R, Bioconductor comprises 934 interoperable packages contributed by a large, diverse community of scientists. Packages cover a range of bioinformatic and statistical applications. They undergo formal initial review and continuous automated testing. We present an overview for prospective users and contributors.","authors":[{"name":"Anders S."},{"name":"Bravo H.C."},{"name":"Carey V.J."},{"name":"Carlson M."},{"name":"Carvalho B.S."},{"name":"Davis S."},{"name":"Gatto L."},{"name":"Gentleman R."},{"name":"Girke T."},{"name":"Gottardo R."},{"name":"Hahne F."},{"name":"Hansen K.D."},{"name":"Huber W."},{"name":"Irizarry R.A."},{"name":"Lawrence M."},{"name":"Love M.I."},{"name":"MaCdonald J."},{"name":"Morgan M."},{"name":"Obenchain V."},{"name":"Oles A.K."},{"name":"Pages H."},{"name":"Reyes A."},{"name":"Shannon P."},{"name":"Smyth G.K."},{"name":"Tenenbaum D."},{"name":"Waldron L."}],"citationCount":2315,"date":"2015-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Orchestrating high-throughput genomic analysis with Bioconductor"},"pmcid":"PMC4509590","pmid":"25633503","type":["Other"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"proFIA","home":"https://bio.tools/profia","license":"CECILL-2.1","version":"1.0.10","summary":"Flow Injection Analysis coupled to High-Resolution Mass Spectrometry is a promising approach for high-throughput metabolomics. FIA-HRMS data, however, cannot be pre-processed with current software tools which rely on liquid chromatography separation, or handle low resolution data only. Here we present the package that implements a new methodology to pre-process FIA-HRMS raw data (netCDF, mzData, mzXML, and mzML) and generates the peak table.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:profia:1.0.10/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_c